# UI I18n Keys Must Be Direct

## Pyramid Layer

- Layer: L1 core UI rule.

## Use This When

- Keep this rule active for any code using `t(...)` style translation calls.

## Stop Here If

- Stop here once direct-key and no-indirection policy is clear.

## Descend To

- No sibling descent required. Apply this rule directly in touched UI code.

## Policy

- Pass translation keys to `t(...)` as direct literals.
- Do not resolve keys through intermediate variables, helper functions, or object indirection.
- Keep key strings visible at call sites so extraction and lint tooling can detect them.

## Prohibited patterns

```ts
const key = 'auth.login.title';
t(key);

const KEYS = { login: 'auth.login.title' };
t(KEYS.login);

function getKey() {
  return 'auth.login.title';
}
t(getKey());
```

## Approved patterns

```ts
t('auth.login.title');
t(`auth.login.title`);
t(isAdmin ? 'admin.title' : 'user.title');
```

## Validation checklist

- `t(...)` first argument is a literal string or a ternary with literal branches.
- No variable/object/function indirection for translation keys.
- Extraction tooling can find all keys in touched files.

## Related rules

- `ui-i18n-json-required`: keys must exist in JSON catalogs under `i18n/`.
